        "abstract": "Field post-stack seismic data often suffer from low resolution and noise corruption due to limitations in seismic acquisition and processing, which undermines reliable seismic interpretation and reservoir characterization.We present SeisGAN-Plus, a generative model that achieves dual improvements in training data and network architecture for simultaneous resolution enhancement and noise suppression of post-stack seismic data. At the data level, we narrow the domain gap between synthetic and field data by incorporating richer structural features during geological modeling and injecting real noise during seismic signal generation, which produces a more realistic training dataset. At the model level, SeisGAN-Plus deepens the generator into a residual-in-residual dense block structure and adopts a relativistic adversarial loss, which enhances feature learning and detail reconstruction capability of the model. Extensive experiments on several synthetic and field datasets confirm that SeisGAN-Plus consistently surpasses conventional workflows and recent deep learning models. Unlike traditional approaches that address resolution enhancement and noise suppression separately, SeisGAN-Plus integrates both tasks within a unified framework, improving efficiency and preserving structural details more effectively. Compared with existing deep learning–based approaches, the high-resolution images generated by SeisGAN-Plus exhibit higher fidelity and avoid common reconstruction problems, such as over-smoothing, amplitude inconsistency, and horizon misalignment. A seismic–well tie validation shows strong agreement between the enhanced traces and the synthetic seismograms derived from actual well logs, demonstrating the reliability of SeisGAN-Plus. Furthermore, SeisGAN-Plus serves as an effective preprocessing strategy for intelligent fault recognition, with a particular advantage in enhancing the identification of small-offset faults that are often difficult to resolve using conventional seismic data. This capability underscores its broad potential for supporting high-precision seismic interpretation and reservoir characterization in complex geological settings.",
